{
    // FI_Standard_FractionalMint.ergo - fractionalization request for an FI bond unit
    // Author: CannonQ (2026)
    //
    // Turns one circulating FI_Standard_Bond unit into N fungible shares backed by
    // FI_Standard_FractionalVault. The layout is ZC_Standard_FractionalMint's; the rules differ:
    // the pull fee must be at least 100000000 nanoERG (0.1 ERG) instead of 2000000, the vault gets
    // exactly 1000000 nanoERG plus the pull fee, both outputs must be freshly stamped, and the
    // owner's co-spend must be younger than the storage-rent age. This script is the only
    // supported creator of FI_Standard_FractionalVault boxes: ZC_Standard_FractionalMint carries
    // none of these stamp, age and value rules.
    // The owner is never assumed to be online after creating this box: everything the mint needs is
    // committed here, so any batcher can run it for the mint fee.
    //
    // CONSTANTS
    // CONST_FRACTIONAL_VAULT_HASH: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of FI_Standard_FractionalVault. That
    //   vault is compiled for one repayment asset, so there is one mint per repayment asset.
    //
    // TOKENS
    // tokens(0): (bond asset, 1) - the only token allowed
    //
    // REGISTERS
    // R4-R6: free. When this box is an order's OUTPUTS(0) they hold the bond asset's EIP-4 data.
    // R7: Coll[Byte] - 32-byte owner script hash, optionally followed by 32 more bytes that no
    //   path reads (a delivery tag in the ZC layout; FI_Standard_LendOffer never delivers here).
    //   The owner receives the shares and may cancel. R7 is read on every path, so a box without
    //   a readable R7 can never be spent.
    // R8: Coll[Long] - (N, pull fee, mint fee):
    //   0 N, the number of shares, 1 <= N <= 1000000000
    //   1 pull batching fee, >= 100000000 nanoERG. It moves into the fractional vault and pays
    //     whoever later pulls the settled bond into it.
    //   2 mint batching fee, >= 2000000 nanoERG. It pays whoever runs the mint.
    // R9: Coll[Coll[Byte]] - the share token's EIP-4 (name, description, decimals), exactly 3 items.
    //   The owner's free choice, fixed here so the minter cannot pick them. Decimals are display
    //   only: every amount on-chain is in raw share units, and no payout granularity is guaranteed.
    //
    // VALUE
    // This box funds three things: the fractional vault (exactly 1000000 nanoERG plus the pull
    // fee), the share output (at least 1000000 nanoERG), and the mint fee. The vault and the share
    // output together receive at least SELF.value minus the mint fee, so every spare nanoERG goes
    // to the share output. A new vault sits at its refresh floor, so its refresh pays no bounty
    // until an absorb adds value.
    //
    // MINT (anyone; no context vars)
    // A transaction mints one token id, INPUTS(0).id, and an order fill already uses it for the
    // bond asset. Shares therefore need this second, chainable transaction.
    // INPUTS(0) = SELF: the share id is this box's id. Exactly 2*N+1 shares are minted.
    // OUTPUTS(0): N shares at tokens(0), at the owner script, at least 1000000 nanoERG, created
    //   at HEIGHT - 1000 or later. R4, R5, R6 = the three items of R9; R7 to R9 are not checked.
    // OUTPUTS(1): FI_Standard_FractionalVault with tokens ((share, N+1), (bond asset, 1)),
    //   R4 = bond asset id, R5: Coll[Long] = (N, N, pull fee), no R6, value exactly 1000000 plus
    //   the pull fee, created at HEIGHT - 1000 or later. The vault's refresh reads R6 as a Byte,
    //   so a register of any other type there would block the refresh until the pull.
    //
    // CANCEL
    // Nothing is minted, and another input whose script hashes to the owner hash releases this
    // box, if that input was created fewer than 1051200 blocks before HEIGHT: an older box can be
    // spent under storage rent without its script running.
    //
    // OWNER SCRIPTS
    // The owner script must be one that only its owner can spend in every instance: P2PK,
    // multisig, or a contract whose keys are compiled-in constants. Anyone can create a box at a
    // script that reads its authority from its own registers, so naming one lets anyone cancel
    // this box and take every payout made to it: a payout pins only its script and a few
    // registers (here the share output, whose R7 to R9 the batcher writes). This script and
    // FI_Standard_FractionalVault can be instantiated by anyone and must never be an owner hash.
    // Builders should refuse any other kind of owner script.
    //
    // VERIFYING A SHARE
    // Share id Y is genuine iff the box with id Y was spent under this exact script and constant,
    // fewer than 1051200 blocks after its creation height: a box that old can be spent under
    // storage rent without its script running.
    // The script then guarantees supply 2*N+1 with N+1 locked in the fractional vault, so for a
    // known (Y, N) "the box holding N+1 units of Y" is the share's state box. Its R4 names the bond
    // asset X; verify X as described in FI_Standard_Order. Also match X's repayment asset to the
    // vault's: the vault takes in coupons only in its own repayment asset, so a bond of another
    // asset wrapped here strands its token coupons. This script does not check that X is a
    // genuine bond: the depositor answers for what they wrap, and share buyers verify it.

    def numTokenInOutputs(tokenId: Coll[Byte]): Long = {
        OUTPUTS.fold(0L, { (a: Long, b: Box) =>
            val count = b.tokens.fold(0L, { (z: Long, t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                if (t._1 == tokenId) z + t._2 else z
            })
            a + count
        })
    }

    val ownerRecord = SELF.R7[Coll[Byte]].get
    val ownerHash = ownerRecord.slice(0, 32)
    val minted = numTokenInOutputs(SELF.id)

    if (minted > 0L) {
        val terms = SELF.R8[Coll[Long]].get
        val metadata = SELF.R9[Coll[Coll[Byte]]].get
        if (terms.size != 3 || metadata.size != 3 || OUTPUTS.size < 2 || SELF.tokens.size != 1) {
            sigmaProp(false)
        } else {
            val shares = terms(0)
            val pullFee = terms(1)
            val mintFee = terms(2)
            val shareOut = OUTPUTS(0)
            val vault = OUTPUTS(1)
            val bondUnit = SELF.tokens(0)

            val termsValid =
                (ownerRecord.size == 32 || ownerRecord.size == 64) &&
                shares >= 1L && shares <= 1000000000L &&
                pullFee >= 100000000L && mintFee >= 2000000L &&
                pullFee <= SELF.value && mintFee <= SELF.value - pullFee

            val mintValid =
                SELF.id == INPUTS(0).id &&
                minted == 2L * shares + 1L &&
                bondUnit._2 == 1L

            val sharesPaid =
                blake2b256(shareOut.propositionBytes) == ownerHash &&
                shareOut.value >= 1000000L &&
                shareOut.tokens.size > 0 &&
                shareOut.tokens(0)._1 == SELF.id && shareOut.tokens(0)._2 == shares &&
                shareOut.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == metadata(0) &&
                shareOut.R5[Coll[Byte]].get == metadata(1) &&
                shareOut.R6[Coll[Byte]].get == metadata(2) &&
                shareOut.creationInfo._1 >= HEIGHT - 1000L

            val vaultValid =
                blake2b256(vault.propositionBytes) == CONST_FRACTIONAL_VAULT_HASH &&
                vault.value - pullFee >= 1000000L &&
                vault.value - pullFee <= 1000000L &&
                vault.value + shareOut.value >= SELF.value - mintFee &&
                vault.tokens == Coll((SELF.id, shares + 1L), bondUnit) &&
                vault.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == bondUnit._1 &&
                vault.R5[Coll[Long]].get == Coll(shares, shares, pullFee) &&
                // No R6: the vault's refresh reads R6 as a Byte, and a register of another type would make
                // that read fail, leaving the box to storage rent until the pull. Registers are dense, so
                // without R6 there is nothing after it either.
                vault.R6[Byte].isDefined == false &&
                vault.creationInfo._1 >= HEIGHT - 1000L

            sigmaProp(termsValid && mintValid && sharesPaid && vaultValid)
        }
    } else {
        val ownerAuth = INPUTS.exists { (b: Box) =>
            b.id != SELF.id && blake2b256(b.propositionBytes) == ownerHash &&
            b.creationInfo._1 > HEIGHT - 1051200
        }
        sigmaProp(ownerAuth)
    }
}
